{"evidence":[{"sentence_id":0,"text":"Fabrice Vetea Santoro (born 9 December 1972) is a retired French professional male tennis player from Tahiti.","title":"Fabrice Santoro"},{"sentence_id":1,"text":" Though not counted among the top-ranked players, he had an unusually long professional career, with many of his accomplishments coming toward the end of his career, and he is popular among spectators and other players alike for his winning demeanor and shot-making abilities.","title":"Fabrice Santoro"},{"sentence_id":0,"text":"2005 Dubai Tennis Championships.","title":"2005 Dubai Tennis Championships – Men's Doubles"},{"sentence_id":1,"text":" Mahesh Bhupathi and Fabrice Santoro were the defending champions.","title":"2005 Dubai Tennis Championships – Men's Doubles"},{"sentence_id":2,"text":" Bhupathi partnered with Todd Woodbridge, losing in the semifinals.","title":"2005 Dubai Tennis Championships – Men's Doubles"},{"sentence_id":3,"text":" Santoro partnered with Jonas Björkman, finishing runner-up.","title":"2005 Dubai Tennis Championships – Men's Doubles"},{"sentence_id":0,"text":"Mahesh Bhupathi and Fabrice Santoro were the defending champions of the doubles event of the Heineken Open tennis tournament, held in Auckland, New Zealand, but did not participate this year.","title":"2005 Heineken Open – Doubles"},{"sentence_id":0,"text":"Snauwaert is Belgian tennis racquet brand and manufacturer of other tennis equipment.","title":"Snauwaert"},{"sentence_id":1,"text":" It was founded in 1928 by the brothers-in-law Valler Snauwaert and Eugeen Depla.","title":"Snauwaert"},{"sentence_id":2,"text":" The company went out of business in 1994.","title":"Snauwaert"},{"sentence_id":3,"text":" Famous tennis players that used Snauwaert include Vitas Gerulaitis, Evonne Goolagong Cawley, Miloslav Mečíř, Mikael Pernfors, Tomáš Šmíd and Brian Gottfried.","title":"Snauwaert"},{"sentence_id":0,"text":"John Letts (born May 11, 1964), is a former professional tennis player from the United States.","title":"John Letts (tennis)"},{"sentence_id":1,"text":" He enjoyed most of his tennis success while playing doubles.","title":"John Letts (tennis)"},{"sentence_id":2,"text":" During his career, he won seven ATP tour doubles titles and reached four ATP tour doubles finals.","title":"John Letts (tennis)"},{"sentence_id":3,"text":" He also reached the quarterfinals of the 1985 Australian Open in doubles knocking out the 3rd seeded team of Tomáš Šmíd and John Fitzgerald in the second round.","title":"John Letts (tennis)"},{"sentence_id":0,"text":"Sergiy Eduardovych Stakhovsky (Ukrainian: Сергій Едуардович Стаховський , ] ; born January 6, 1986) is a Ukrainian professional tennis player.","title":"Sergiy Stakhovsky"},{"sentence_id":1,"text":" Stakhovsky turned professional in 2003 and had been playing mostly at the Challenger level from 2005–2008.","title":"Sergiy Stakhovsky"},{"sentence_id":2,"text":" His career-high singles ranking is World No. 31 (September 2010) and he has reached as high as No. 33 in doubles the same month.","title":"Sergiy Stakhovsky"},{"sentence_id":3,"text":" He won his first career title in March 2008, as a lucky loser ranked no. 209, defeating top seed Ivan Ljubičić in the final, thus becoming the first lucky loser to win a title since Christian Miniussi in 1991.","title":"Sergiy Stakhovsky"},{"sentence_id":4,"text":" He is the elder brother of tennis player Leonard Stakhovsky.","title":"Sergiy Stakhovsky"},{"sentence_id":5,"text":" He is currently coached by Fabrice Santoro.","title":"Sergiy Stakhovsky"},{"sentence_id":6,"text":" He is well known for beating seven-time winner and defending champion Roger Federer in the 2nd round of the 2013 Wimbledon Championships ending his record run of 36 consecutive Grand Slam quarterfinals.","title":"Sergiy Stakhovsky"}],"peer_messages":["Unverified peer answer: Yes
